<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!-- ====================================================================
       ORBIT: ALWAYS VIEWABLE

       PlanetLayerDef defaults viewGizmoOnlyVisibleWithDirectConnection to
       true, and Odyssey's Orbit layer does not override it. The "view orbit"
       button therefore only appears once you have a presence up there -
       which means that for the entire pre-gravship game you cannot look at
       space at all, and cannot confirm anything generated in it.

       Flipping it to false makes the view-orbit gizmo always available on
       the world map.

       This is VIEWING ONLY. Reaching orbit is gated separately and
       independently: SpaceSettlement sets requiresSignalJammerToReach, and
       you still need a gravship to travel there. Nothing here lets you
       arrive anywhere early.

       Two reasons to keep it:
         - Verification. Without it there is no way to check that orbit
           generated correctly, or that orbital factions got placed, short
           of playing for many hours.
         - Theme. Being able to look up at the stations you cannot reach
           yet, from a neolithic camp, is the whole premise of the run.

       If you would rather have the vanilla reveal-on-arrival behaviour,
       delete this file. Nothing else depends on it.
       ==================================================================== -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/PlanetLayerDef[defName="Orbit"]</xpath>
    <value>
      <viewGizmoOnlyVisibleWithDirectConnection>false</viewGizmoOnlyVisibleWithDirectConnection>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
